      "worked": "For real square roots, $a,b\\ge0$. The denominator is nonzero only when $a\\ne b$. Otherwise the original expression is undefined over the reals.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sqrt a+\\sqrt b}{\\sqrt a-\\sqrt b}&=\\frac{(\\sqrt a+\\sqrt b)^2}{(\\sqrt a-\\sqrt b)(\\sqrt a+\\sqrt b)}\\\\\\frac{\\sqrt a+\\sqrt b}{\\sqrt a-\\sqrt b}&=\\frac{a+2\\sqrt{ab}+b}{a-b}\\end{align*}$$",
